            "This spell reduces the sun s light to a comfortable glow in a stationary area, dropping the temperature by 20 degrees. Creatures inside the effect gain a one-step improvement in protection against heat, are not subject to sunburn, and can begin to recover from sun glare and nonlethal damage due to heat (see Chapter 1). Impede sun s brilliance has no effect on light, daylight, sunburst, and similar magical light effects, and it offers no protection from damage that creatures vulnerable to sunlight might take from the sun.<br>"
