            "Any creature that bites the spell's subject must succeed on a Fortitude saving throw or be nauseated until the end of its next turn.<br><br>",
            "If a creature of animal Intelligence (2 or lower) fails its saving throw, it will not willingly bite the subject a second time; someone trying to direct the creature to bite the subject again must make a Handle Animal check as if he was trying to 'push' the creature. This check must be made every time he tries to make the creature bite.<br><br>",
